The access to LLVM is guarded by Python locks so that only one thread may access the LLVM machinery at a time. After numerous thread safety fixes were applied in different parts of the compilation chain a unified fix between llvmlite and Numba went in [here](https://github.com/numba/numba/pull/2627) and [here](https://github.com/numba/llvmlite/pull/318). The main compiler pipeline entry points are also guarded by Python locks.

I don't *think* `atomic_cas` is in use any more, it was used in the spin lock in the NRT a while back but looking through the code now I'm unconvinced it is needed.

