@lhames Beware, I just edited the patch up there to strengthen two of the `if`s to ensure that `Value.SectionID == SectionID` is only considered if `AbiVariant == 2`, and thus to keep my promise only to affect ELFv2.

I believe that where a weak function definition is overridden by a stronger one in the same object file, the compiler already has the insight it needs to properly set and restore `r2`, because those are going to be intra-Object calls and the compiler does know which functions share a TOC pointer and which don't.

What the RuntimeDyld wasn't noticing, and what this patch causes it to notice, is that if code sections come from different objects, they are guaranteed _not_ to share a TOC pointer.

